   "h": "Main crops and where they grow",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 188\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"65\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"42.5\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Crop</text><rect x=\"75\" y=\"6\" width=\"125\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"137.5\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Needs</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"6\" width=\"110\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Top states</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"32\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"42.5\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Rice</text><rect x=\"75\" y=\"32\" width=\"125\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"137.5\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25 C, 100+ cm rain</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"32\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">WB, UP, Punjab</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"62\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"42.5\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Wheat</text><rect x=\"75\" y=\"62\" width=\"125\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"137.5\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cool, 50-75 cm rain</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"62\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">UP, MP, Punjab</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"92\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"42.5\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Cotton</text><rect x=\"75\" y=\"92\" width=\"125\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"137.5\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Black soil, 21-30 C</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"92\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gujarat, Maharashtra</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"122\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"42.5\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Sugarcane</text><rect x=\"75\" y=\"122\" width=\"125\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"137.5\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hot, wet, 75-150 cm</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"122\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">UP, Maharashtra</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"152\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"42.5\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Tea</text><rect x=\"75\" y=\"152\" width=\"125\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"137.5\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hill slopes, 150 cm</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"152\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Assam, WB, Kerala</text></svg><p>Crops follow rainfall, temperature and soil. <b>Rice</b> is the staple of the east and south. <b>Wheat</b> dominates the north-west. <b>Millets</b> (shree anna) grow in dry regions; 2023 was the International Year of Millets.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Cash and plantation crops",
   "b": "<p><b>Cotton</b> and <b>jute</b> are fibres; jute grows in the Ganga-Brahmaputra delta of West Bengal. <b>Sugarcane</b> is needed for sugar mills. <b>Tea</b> (Assam), <b>coffee</b> (Karnataka, Kodagu) and <b>rubber</b> (Kerala) are plantations. India is the second largest producer of tea and of rice, wheat and sugar too, as of recent data.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Irrigation",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 132\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"105\" height=\"36\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"62.5\" y=\"28.0\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Canals</text><rect x=\"121\" y=\"6\" width=\"189\" height=\"36\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.5\" y=\"28.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">North Indian plains, Punjab, UP, delta</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"48\" width=\"105\" height=\"36\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dceaec\" stroke=\"#2f6f7a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"62.5\" y=\"70.0\" fill=\"#2f6f7a\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Wells and tubewells</text><rect x=\"121\" y=\"48\" width=\"189\" height=\"36\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.5\" y=\"70.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Plains and Deccan, about 60% of irrigated area</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"90\" width=\"105\" height=\"36\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4dcd5\" stroke=\"#a3362a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"62.5\" y=\"112.0\" fill=\"#a3362a\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Tanks</text><rect x=\"121\" y=\"90\" width=\"189\" height=\"36\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.5\" y=\"112.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peninsula, rocky land, Tamil Nadu, Andhra</text></svg><p>Net irrigated area is about 55% of net sown area. Wells and tubewells lead because they are cheap and farmer-controlled, but they deplete the groundwater table. Tanks are common where rock is hard. Drip and sprinkler systems save water.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "The Green Revolution",
   "b": "<p>From the mid-1960s, <b>HYV seeds</b> (Norman Borlaug; M.S. Swaminathan in India), fertiliser, irrigation and credit raised wheat and then rice output in Punjab, Haryana and western UP. India became self-sufficient in food grains. Limits: regional and crop bias, soil degradation, falling water tables.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Debate",
   "h": "Is the Punjab model sustainable?",
   "b": "<p>Punjab and Haryana grow rice in a dry region because MSP and procurement favour it. Groundwater falls about a metre a year in some blocks, and stubble burning pollutes Delhi. Experts urge <b>crop diversification</b> to pulses, maize and oilseeds, direct-seeded rice and price signals. Others warn farmers will not shift without assured purchase.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Policy at a glance",
   "b": "<p><b>MSP</b> is declared by the Centre on CACP advice for 22 crops plus FRP for sugarcane. <b>PM-KISAN</b> (2019) gives cash. <b>PMFBY</b> (2016) is crop insurance. <b>e-NAM</b> links mandis. The three farm laws were repealed in 2021 after farmer protests. The government's target is to double farmer income, widely seen as missed.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Indian angle",
   "h": "New frontiers",
   "b": "<p>Horticulture output now exceeds food grains. <b>Operation Flood</b> (1970) made India the largest milk producer. The Northeast and Odisha show <b>jhum</b> being replaced slowly. <b>Natural farming</b> mission launched in 2024 and drone use (Namo Drone Didi) are fresh themes. The <b>Kharif</b> crops depend on monsoon; Rabi on stored moisture and irrigation.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Exam lens",
   "cls": "exam",
   "h": "How to write this",
   "b": "<div class=\"box\"><h4>Likely questions</h4><p>\"Discuss the changing cropping pattern in India and its causes.\" (10 marks)</p><p>\"Examine the importance of irrigation in Indian agriculture.\" (10 marks)</p></div><p><b>Structure:</b> trend in numbers; physical factors; policy factors (MSP, irrigation); impact (water, soil); way forward.</p><p><b>Prelims tip:</b> match crops to seasons and states; rice is kharif; wheat is rabi; MSP is set on CACP advice.</p>"
  }
 ],
